From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:02:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-dai: a push-pull stream is not a batch PCM

q6apm-dai marks every PCM SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH, but a push-pull graph takes its
pointer from the position buffer the DSP updates every processing frame, not only at
period ends. Clear the flag for those graphs, so user space stops padding them with a
period of extra buffering.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -400,6 +400,10 @@
 		runtime->hw = q6apm_dai_hardware_playback;
 	else if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE)
 		runtime->hw = q6apm_dai_hardware_capture;
+
+	/* A push-pull graph reports the DSP's own position, not only period ends */
+	if (q6apm_is_graph_in_push_pull_mode(prtd->graph))
+		runtime->hw.info &= ~SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH;
 
 	/* Ensure that buffer size is a multiple of period size */
 	ret = snd_pcm_hw_constraint_integer(runtime, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_PERIODS);
